+# FAQ for newcomers
+
+## How do I install the command line tool?
+
+Install it with pipx (Python 3.11 or newer): `pipx install tally-toolkit`. If the command is then not found, run
+`pipx ensurepath` and open a new terminal.
+
+## What is the tool called now?
+
+`tallyctl`. It was `tally-cli` until the 2026-09 release; the old name works as an alias for one more release only.
+
+## Which port does tally listen on?
+
+Port 8731. The old port 8080 is closed, so anything still using it gets a refused connection.
+
+## How do I clear the cache?
+
+Run `tallyctl cache clear`, which clears all regions; add `--region NAME` for just one. The old purge command was
+removed.
+
+## How long until an unanswered page escalates?
+
+15 minutes without acknowledgement. It goes from the primary to the secondary, then to the engineering manager.
+
+## Does the pager wake me at night?
+
+Only for severity 1 (customer-facing data loss or a full outage) between 22:00 and 07:00. Severity 2 waits until
+morning.
+
+## What do I do when the ingest queue is stuck?
+
+Restart ingest with a drain first, and look for the cause afterwards: `tallyctl restart ingest --drain`. It parks the
+stuck batch in the dead-letter table.
+
+## What do I do when the API certificate has expired?
+
+Renew it, then restart the API, because the new certificate is only served after a restart: `tallyctl certs renew api`,
+then `tallyctl restart api`.
